<title>SPAIN: Spain Mar CPI rose 0.1 pct m/m, 2.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Spain Mar CPI rose 0.1 pct m/m, 2.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute (INE) gave the following figures:</p>
<p> SPANISH INFLATION		MAR 97    FEB 97   MAR 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change	0.1	-0.1	0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 2.2	 2.5	3.4</p>
<p> Core inflation		    0.2	 0.1	0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 2.1	 2.3	4.2</p>
<p> INDEX BY COMPONENTS	     MAR 97     FEB 97     YR/YR</p>
<p> Food				  -0.3	 -0.8	  1.0</p>
<p> Clothing			     0.1	  0.0	  2.1</p>
<p> Housing				0.1	  0.2	  3.3</p>
<p> Household goods		    0.2	  0.3	  2.3</p>
<p> Medicine			    -0.1	  0.8	  3.0</p>
<p> Transport			    0.0	  0.1	  2.4</p>
<p> Culture				0.1	  0.2	  2.1</p>
<p> Other				  0.7	  0.3	  3.5</p>
<p>Note - In food, fresh food fell 0.9 pct from the previous month (2.2 pct year-on-year) and processed food was unchanged from the previous month (rose 0.2 pct year-on-year)</p>
</text>
